      "math": "L(\\theta) = -\\frac{1}{N} \\sum_{i=1}^N \\log P(y_i \\mid x_i; \\theta)",
      "examTip": "Always write down both the single-sample loss L and the batch cost function J.",
      "completeAnswer": "### 1. Executive Definition & Core Principles\nComprehensive academic examination of Relationship Framework: Logits, Sigmoid, Softmax and Cross-Entropy.\n\n### 2. Comprehensive Theoretical Mechanism & Architecture\nIn university descriptive examinations, answering 'Explain the relationship between logits, sigmoid, softmax and cross-entropy.' requires defining the mathematical formulation, error geometry, gradient derivation, and appropriate task selection.\n\n### 3. Mathematical Formulation & Key Equations\n$$L(\\theta) = -\\frac{1}{N} \\sum_{i=1}^N \\log P(y_i \\mid x_i; \\theta)$$\n- Provides the exact analytical relationship governing parameter trajectories and loss gradients.\n\n### 4. Key Examination Takeaways & Practical Insights\n- **Mathematical Formulation & Range**: Mathematical Formulation & Range\n- **Probabilistic Foundation (Maximum Likelihood Estimation)**: Probabilistic Foundation (Maximum Likelihood Estimation)\n- **Gradient Behavior during Backpropagation**: Gradient Behavior during Backpropagation\n- **Practical Guidelines for Model Selection**: Practical Guidelines for Model Selection"
