    "svg": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 740 320\" width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\" class=\"diagram-svg\">\n      \n    <defs>\n      <linearGradient id=\"bgGrad\" x1=\"0%\" y1=\"0%\" x2=\"100%\" y2=\"100%\">\n        <stop offset=\"0%\" stop-color=\"#0f172a\"/>\n        <stop offset=\"100%\" stop-color=\"#1e1e38\"/>\n      </linearGradient>\n      <linearGradient id=\"primaryGrad\" x1=\"0%\" y1=\"0%\" x2=\"100%\" y2=\"100%\">\n        <stop offset=\"0%\" stop-color=\"#6366f1\"/>\n        <stop offset=\"100%\" stop-color=\"#8b5cf6\"/>\n      </linearGradient>\n      <linearGradient id=\"cyanGrad\" x1=\"0%\" y1=\"0%\" x2=\"100%\" y2=\"100%\">\n        <stop offset=\"0%\" stop-color=\"#06b6d4\"/>\n        <stop offset=\"100%\" stop-color=\"#3b82f6\"/>\n      </linearGradient>\n      <linearGradient id=\"emeraldGrad\" x1=\"0%\" y1=\"0%\" x2=\"100%\" y2=\"100%\">\n        <stop offset=\"0%\" stop-color=\"#10b981\"/>\n        <stop offset=\"100%\" stop-color=\"#059669\"/>\n      </linearGradient>\n      <linearGradient id=\"amberGrad\" x1=\"0%\" y1=\"0%\" x2=\"100%\" y2=\"100%\">\n        <stop offset=\"0%\" stop-color=\"#f59e0b\"/>\n        <stop offset=\"100%\" stop-color=\"#d97706\"/>\n      </linearGradient>\n      <linearGradient id=\"roseGrad\" x1=\"0%\" y1=\"0%\" x2=\"100%\" y2=\"100%\">\n        <stop offset=\"0%\" stop-color=\"#f43f5e\"/>\n        <stop offset=\"100%\" stop-color=\"#e11d48\"/>\n      </linearGradient>\n      <filter id=\"glow\" x=\"-20%\" y=\"-20%\" width=\"140%\" height=\"140%\">\n        <feGaussianBlur stdDeviation=\"4\" result=\"blur\" />\n        <feComposite in=\"SourceGraphic\" in2=\"blur\" operator=\"over\" />\n      </filter>\n      <marker id=\"arrow\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"8\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"6\" markerHeight=\"6\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\">\n        <path d=\"M 0 1 L 10 5 L 0 9 z\" fill=\"#94a3b8\" />\n      </marker>\n      <marker id=\"arrow-cyan\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"8\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"6\" markerHeight=\"6\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\">\n        <path d=\"M 0 1 L 10 5 L 0 9 z\" fill=\"#38bdf8\" />\n      </marker>\n      <marker id=\"arrow-emerald\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"8\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"6\" markerHeight=\"6\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\">\n        <path d=\"M 0 1 L 10 5 L 0 9 z\" fill=\"#34d399\" />\n      </marker>\n      <marker id=\"arrow-rose\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"8\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"6\" markerHeight=\"6\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\">\n        <path d=\"M 0 1 L 10 5 L 0 9 z\" fill=\"#fb7185\" />\n      </marker>\n    </defs>\n    \n      <rect width=\"740\" height=\"320\" rx=\"16\" fill=\"url(#bgGrad)\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n      \n        <rect x=\"20\" y=\"16\" width=\"700\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#1e293b\" fill-opacity=\"0.8\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n        <circle cx=\"36\" cy=\"33\" r=\"5\" fill=\"#6366f1\"/>\n        <text x=\"50\" y=\"38\" fill=\"#f8fafc\" font-size=\"14\" font-family=\"system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif\" font-weight=\"600\">Question 132: Numerical AdaGrad Cumulative Variance Step</text>\n        \n      \n    <!-- Elliptical ravine contours -->\n    <ellipse cx=\"380\" cy=\"180\" rx=\"300\" ry=\"85\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n    <ellipse cx=\"380\" cy=\"180\" rx=\"220\" ry=\"60\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n    <ellipse cx=\"380\" cy=\"180\" rx=\"140\" ry=\"38\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n    <ellipse cx=\"380\" cy=\"180\" rx=\"60\" ry=\"18\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n    <circle cx=\"380\" cy=\"180\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#10b981\" filter=\"url(#glow)\"/>\n    <text x=\"380\" y=\"165\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#34d399\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"700\">Optimum w*</text>\n    \n    <!-- Start Point -->\n    <circle cx=\"120\" cy=\"240\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#ffffff\"/>\n    <text x=\"105\" y=\"260\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"700\">Start (w₀)</text>\n    \n    <!-- Standard SGD Path (high oscillation) -->\n    <path d=\"M 120 240 L 150 120 L 180 235 L 210 125 L 240 225 L 270 135 L 300 215 L 330 145\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#f43f5e\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"3,2\"/>\n    <text x=\"180\" y=\"110\" fill=\"#fb7185\" font-size=\"10\" font-weight=\"700\">Standard SGD (Oscillates!)</text>\n    \n    <!-- Advanced Optimizer Path -->\n    <path d=\"M 120 240 Q 180 195, 260 185 T 375 180\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#38bdf8\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" filter=\"url(#glow)\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow-cyan)\"/>\n    <text x=\"270\" y=\"172\" fill=\"#38bdf8\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"700\">AdaGrad Step (Accelerated Direct Path!)</text>\n    \n    <!-- Feature Description Card -->\n    <rect x=\"50\" y=\"65\" width=\"220\" height=\"60\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#1e293b\" stroke=\"#38bdf8\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n    <text x=\"65\" y=\"85\" fill=\"#38bdf8\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"700\">Pathological Curvature:</text>\n    <text x=\"65\" y=\"100\" fill=\"#94a3b8\" font-size=\"10\">• Steep walls (high eigenvalue)</text>\n    <text x=\"65\" y=\"114\" fill=\"#94a3b8\" font-size=\"10\">• Gentle valley floor (low eigenvalue)</text>\n    \n    <!-- Remedy Card -->\n    <rect x=\"480\" y=\"65\" width=\"210\" height=\"60\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#1e293b\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n    <text x=\"495\" y=\"85\" fill=\"#34d399\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"700\">Momentum / Adam Remedy:</text>\n    <text x=\"495\" y=\"100\" fill=\"#94a3b8\" font-size=\"10\">• Cancels perpendicular oscillations</text>\n    <text x=\"495\" y=\"114\" fill=\"#94a3b8\" font-size=\"10\">• Accelerates down shallow valley</text>\n    \n    </svg>",
    "solution": {
      "concept": "Exhaustive academic breakdown of Loss Landscapes: Geometry, Ravines, Curvature & Visualization.",
      "theory": "In descriptive university examinations, answering 'What is a loss landscape?' requires explaining the convergence properties, hyperparameter tuning, mathematical update equations, and comparative advantages.",
      "points": [
        "Mathematical Formulation & Update Equations",
        "Convergence Speed & Stability Analysis",
        "Handling Ravines, Oscillations and Ill-Conditioning",
        "Practical Implementation & Default Hyperparameters"
      ],
      "math": "\\theta_{t+1} = \\theta_t - \\frac{\\eta}{\\sqrt{\\hat{v}_t} + \\epsilon} \\hat{m}_t",
      "examTip": "For optimizer questions, always compare against Vanilla SGD as a baseline to highlight what specific limitation the optimizer resolves.",
      "completeAnswer": "### 1. Executive Definition & Core Principles\nExhaustive academic breakdown of Loss Landscapes: Geometry, Ravines, Curvature & Visualization.\n\n### 2. Comprehensive Theoretical Mechanism & Architecture\nIn descriptive university examinations, answering 'What is a loss landscape?' requires explaining the convergence properties, hyperparameter tuning, mathematical update equations, and comparative advantages.\n\n### 3. Mathematical Formulation & Key Equations\n$$\\theta_{t+1} = \\theta_t - \\frac{\\eta}{\\sqrt{\\hat{v}_t} + \\epsilon} \\hat{m}_t$$\n- Provides the exact analytical relationship governing parameter trajectories and loss gradients.\n\n### 4. Key Examination Takeaways & Practical Insights\n- **Mathematical Formulation & Update Equations**: Mathematical Formulation & Update Equations\n- **Convergence Speed & Stability Analysis**: Convergence Speed & Stability Analysis\n- **Handling Ravines, Oscillations and Ill-Conditioning**: Handling Ravines, Oscillations and Ill-Conditioning\n- **Practical Implementation & Default Hyperparameters**: Practical Implementation & Default Hyperparameters"
    }
