      "completeAnswer": "### 1. Executive Definition & Core Principles\nComprehensive academic examination of Comparative Analysis: Binary vs Multiclass Classification.\n\n### 2. Comprehensive Theoretical Mechanism & Architecture\nIn university descriptive examinations, answering 'Differentiate binary and multiclass classification.' involves analyzing the confusion matrix, mathematical definitions, geometric interpretation, and failure modes.\n\n### 3. Mathematical Formulation & Key Equations\n$$\\text{Precision} = \\frac{TP}{TP+FP}; \\quad \\text{Recall} = \\frac{TP}{TP+FN}; \\quad F_1 = \\frac{2 \\cdot P \\cdot R}{P + R}$$\n- Dictates the analytical relationship governing representations and gradients.\n\n### 4. Key Examination Takeaways & Practical Insights\n- **Mathematical Definition & Formula**: Mathematical Definition & Formula\n- **Confusion Matrix Mapping (TP, FP, FN, TN)**: Confusion Matrix Mapping (TP, FP, FN, TN)\n- **Vulnerability to Skewed Class Distributions**: Vulnerability to Skewed Class Distributions\n- **Real-World Domain Selection (e.g. Medical Diagnosis vs Search)**: Real-World Domain Selection (e.g. Medical Diagnosis vs Search)"
