      "completeAnswer": "### 1. Executive Definition & Core Principles\nEngineering diagnosis and production deep learning solution for Application Problem 3: Dataset Splitting Strategy for 100K Samples & 50 Features.\n\n### 2. Comprehensive Theoretical Mechanism & Architecture\nAddressing 'Application Problem 3: A Kaggle dataset has 100,000 samples and 50 features. Explain how you would divide the dataset into training, validation, and test sets.' requires a structured diagnostic protocol: symptom identification, root cause analysis, mathematical grounding, and at least five concrete actionable remedies.\n\n### 3. Mathematical Formulation & Key Equations\n$$\\text{Generalization Gap} = \\mathcal{L}_{val}(\\theta) - \\mathcal{L}_{train}(\\theta)$$\n- Dictates the analytical relationship governing representations and gradients.\n\n### 4. Key Examination Takeaways & Practical Insights\n- **Problem Diagnosis & Identification of Failure Mode**: Problem Diagnosis & Identification of Failure Mode\n- **Root Causes (Data quality, capacity mismatch, optimization stagnation, distribution shift)**: Root Causes (Data quality, capacity mismatch, optimization stagnation, distribution shift)\n- **Step-by-Step Remediation Plan (Regularization, architectures, optimizers)**: Step-by-Step Remediation Plan (Regularization, architectures, optimizers)\n- **Monitoring & Validation Strategy (Early stopping, learning rate decay)**: Monitoring & Validation Strategy (Early stopping, learning rate decay)"
