      "math": "\\frac{\\partial L}{\\partial W^{[l]}} = \\delta^{[l]} (a^{[l-1]})^T; \\quad W^{[l]} \\leftarrow W^{[l]} - \\eta \\frac{\\partial L}{\\partial W^{[l]}}",
      "examTip": "Write out the numerical values neatly at each step to prevent arithmetic errors from cascading into subsequent layers.",
      "completeAnswer": "### 1. Executive Definition & Core Principles\nFull step-by-step mathematical derivation and gradient backpropagation for Comprehensive Problem 2: Two-Layer ReLU Network Complete Forward, Loss & Backpropagation Step.\n\n### 2. Comprehensive Theoretical Mechanism & Architecture\nEvaluating the computational graph layer-by-layer, computing pre-activations, post-activations, scalar loss, local Jacobian matrices, and gradient descent parameter updates.\n\n### 3. Mathematical Formulation & Key Equations\n$$\\frac{\\partial L}{\\partial W^{[l]}} = \\delta^{[l]} (a^{[l-1]})^T; \\quad W^{[l]} \\leftarrow W^{[l]} - \\eta \\frac{\\partial L}{\\partial W^{[l]}}$$\n- Dictates the analytical relationship governing representations and gradients.\n\n### 4. Key Examination Takeaways & Practical Insights\n- **Forward Pass**:  Sequential evaluation of each intermediate node\n- **Backward Pass**:  Reverse topological chain rule traversal\n- **Parameter Gradients**:  Outer product of upstream delta and layer inputs\n- **Verification**:  Ensuring loss decreases after gradient step"
