      "completeAnswer": "### 1. Executive Definition & Core Principles\nComprehensive, university-exam 15-mark exhaustive solution for Long-Answer Problem 8: Comprehensive Mathematical Comparison of Sigmoid, Tanh, ReLU, and Leaky ReLU.\n\n### 2. Comprehensive Theoretical Mechanism & Architecture\nAddressing 'Long-Answer Problem 8: Compare sigmoid, tanh, ReLU, and Leaky ReLU mathematically, including their derivatives, advantages, disadvantages, and suitability for different layers.' as a high-weightage descriptive exam question requires an essay-structured response with clear subheadings, mathematical derivations from first principles, comparative tables, architectural diagrams, and empirical justifications.\n\n### 3. Mathematical Formulation & Key Equations\n$$\\mathcal{L}(\\theta) = \\frac{1}{N} \\sum_{i=1}^N \\ell(f(x_i; \\theta), y_i) + \\lambda \\Omega(\\theta)$$\n- Dictates the analytical relationship governing representations and gradients.\n\n### 4. Key Examination Takeaways & Practical Insights\n- **Part 1**:  Executive Summary & Theoretical Context\n- **Part 2**:  Rigorous Mathematical Formulations & Derivations\n- **Part 3**:  Comparative Analysis Matrix with Trade-offs\n- **Part 4**:  Architectural Flowchart & Signal Propagation\n- **Part 5**:  Production Best Practices & Common Examination Pitfalls"
