    "question": "Long-Answer Problem 10: A neural network is suffering from vanishing gradients and overfitting simultaneously. Propose a systematic strategy to address both problems and justify each modification.",
    "svg": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 740 320\" width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\" class=\"diagram-svg\">\n      \n    <defs>\n      <linearGradient id=\"bgGrad\" x1=\"0%\" y1=\"0%\" x2=\"100%\" y2=\"100%\">\n        <stop offset=\"0%\" stop-color=\"#0f172a\"/>\n        <stop offset=\"100%\" stop-color=\"#1e1e38\"/>\n      </linearGradient>\n      <linearGradient id=\"primaryGrad\" x1=\"0%\" y1=\"0%\" x2=\"100%\" y2=\"100%\">\n        <stop offset=\"0%\" stop-color=\"#6366f1\"/>\n        <stop offset=\"100%\" stop-color=\"#8b5cf6\"/>\n      </linearGradient>\n      <linearGradient id=\"cyanGrad\" x1=\"0%\" y1=\"0%\" x2=\"100%\" y2=\"100%\">\n        <stop offset=\"0%\" stop-color=\"#06b6d4\"/>\n        <stop offset=\"100%\" stop-color=\"#3b82f6\"/>\n      </linearGradient>\n      <linearGradient id=\"emeraldGrad\" x1=\"0%\" y1=\"0%\" x2=\"100%\" y2=\"100%\">\n        <stop offset=\"0%\" stop-color=\"#10b981\"/>\n        <stop offset=\"100%\" stop-color=\"#059669\"/>\n      </linearGradient>\n      <linearGradient id=\"amberGrad\" x1=\"0%\" y1=\"0%\" x2=\"100%\" y2=\"100%\">\n        <stop offset=\"0%\" stop-color=\"#f59e0b\"/>\n        <stop offset=\"100%\" stop-color=\"#d97706\"/>\n      </linearGradient>\n      <linearGradient id=\"roseGrad\" x1=\"0%\" y1=\"0%\" x2=\"100%\" y2=\"100%\">\n        <stop offset=\"0%\" stop-color=\"#f43f5e\"/>\n        <stop offset=\"100%\" stop-color=\"#e11d48\"/>\n      </linearGradient>\n      <filter id=\"glow\" x=\"-20%\" y=\"-20%\" width=\"140%\" height=\"140%\">\n        <feGaussianBlur stdDeviation=\"4\" result=\"blur\" />\n        <feComposite in=\"SourceGraphic\" in2=\"blur\" operator=\"over\" />\n      </filter>\n      <marker id=\"arrow\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"8\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"6\" markerHeight=\"6\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\">\n        <path d=\"M 0 1 L 10 5 L 0 9 z\" fill=\"#94a3b8\" />\n      </marker>\n      <marker id=\"arrow-cyan\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"8\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"6\" markerHeight=\"6\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\">\n        <path d=\"M 0 1 L 10 5 L 0 9 z\" fill=\"#38bdf8\" />\n      </marker>\n      <marker id=\"arrow-emerald\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"8\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"6\" markerHeight=\"6\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\">\n        <path d=\"M 0 1 L 10 5 L 0 9 z\" fill=\"#34d399\" />\n      </marker>\n      <marker id=\"arrow-rose\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"8\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"6\" markerHeight=\"6\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\">\n        <path d=\"M 0 1 L 10 5 L 0 9 z\" fill=\"#fb7185\" />\n      </marker>\n    </defs>\n    \n      <rect width=\"740\" height=\"320\" rx=\"16\" fill=\"url(#bgGrad)\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n      \n        <rect x=\"20\" y=\"16\" width=\"700\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#1e293b\" fill-opacity=\"0.8\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n        <circle cx=\"36\" cy=\"33\" r=\"5\" fill=\"#6366f1\"/>\n        <text x=\"50\" y=\"38\" fill=\"#f8fafc\" font-size=\"14\" font-family=\"system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif\" font-weight=\"600\">Long-Answer 10: Systematic Engineering Strategy for Simultaneous Vanishing Gradients &amp; Overfitting</text>\n        \n      \n    <g transform=\"translate(40, 85)\">\n      <!-- Step 1: Mini-batch Mean -->\n      <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"140\" height=\"135\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#1e293b\" stroke=\"#38bdf8\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n      <text x=\"70\" y=\"25\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#38bdf8\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"700\">1. Mini-Batch Mean</text>\n      <rect x=\"15\" y=\"45\" width=\"110\" height=\"40\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#0f172a\"/>\n      <text x=\"70\" y=\"70\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\">μ_B = 1/m ∑ xᵢ</text>\n      <text x=\"70\" y=\"105\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#94a3b8\" font-size=\"10\">Tracks batch centroid</text>\n      \n      <line x1=\"145\" y1=\"67\" x2=\"175\" y2=\"67\" stroke=\"#64748b\" stroke-width=\"2\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow)\"/>\n      \n      <!-- Step 2: Mini-batch Variance -->\n      <rect x=\"180\" y=\"0\" width=\"140\" height=\"135\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#1e293b\" stroke=\"#818cf8\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n      <text x=\"250\" y=\"25\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#818cf8\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"700\">2. Batch Variance</text>\n      <rect x=\"195\" y=\"45\" width=\"110\" height=\"40\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#0f172a\"/>\n      <text x=\"250\" y=\"70\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\">σ_B² = 1/m ∑(xᵢ-μ)²</text>\n      <text x=\"250\" y=\"105\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#94a3b8\" font-size=\"10\">Dispersion measure</text>\n      \n      <line x1=\"325\" y1=\"67\" x2=\"355\" y2=\"67\" stroke=\"#64748b\" stroke-width=\"2\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow)\"/>\n      \n      <!-- Step 3: Zero-mean unit-variance -->\n      <rect x=\"360\" y=\"0\" width=\"140\" height=\"135\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#1e293b\" stroke=\"#fbbf24\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n      <text x=\"430\" y=\"25\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fbbf24\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"700\">3. Normalize</text>\n      <rect x=\"375\" y=\"45\" width=\"110\" height=\"40\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#0f172a\"/>\n      <text x=\"430\" y=\"70\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\">x̂ᵢ = (xᵢ-μ)/√(σ²+ε)</text>\n      <text x=\"430\" y=\"105\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#94a3b8\" font-size=\"10\">Zero mean, unit variance</text>\n      \n      <line x1=\"505\" y1=\"67\" x2=\"535\" y2=\"67\" stroke=\"#64748b\" stroke-width=\"2\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow)\"/>\n      \n      <!-- Step 4: Scale and Shift -->\n      <rect x=\"540\" y=\"0\" width=\"140\" height=\"135\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#1e293b\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n      <text x=\"610\" y=\"25\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#34d399\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"700\">4. Scale &amp; Shift</text>\n      <rect x=\"555\" y=\"45\" width=\"110\" height=\"40\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#0f172a\"/>\n      <text x=\"610\" y=\"70\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\">yᵢ = γ · x̂ᵢ + β</text>\n      <text x=\"610\" y=\"105\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#94a3b8\" font-size=\"10\">Learnable γ and β!</text>\n    </g>\n    \n    <!-- Bottom Summary -->\n    <rect x=\"40\" y=\"250\" width=\"660\" height=\"45\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#0f172a\" stroke=\"#38bdf8\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n    <text x=\"370\" y=\"268\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#38bdf8\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"700\">\n      Mitigates Internal Covariate Shift • Enables Higher Learning Rates • Serves as Gentle Regularizer\n    </text>\n    <text x=\"370\" y=\"285\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#94a3b8\" font-size=\"10\">\n      At test time, running population statistics (E[x] and Var[x]) are fixed for deterministic inference.\n    </text>\n    \n    </svg>",
